From 9defc27b9aa59a7200abfad80f5ae7c4885a2449 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:13:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(coreelec): keep the refresh rate while a video fills
 the screen

YouTube makes the player again for the same video (e.g. right after it
starts). The old player's end scheduled the return to the normal refresh
rate, and nothing cancelled it, since TizenTube asks for a rate only when
playback starts: five seconds later the TV went back to 60 Hz mid-video.
Count the full-screen videos (from each player's bounds): while one shows,
the display keeps its rate, and the return is due five seconds after the
last one goes. Home screen previews are windows and do not count.
